<title>CHILE: Chile's CTC signs $315 million loan.</title>
<headline>Chile's CTC signs $315 million loan.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Compania de Telecomunicaciones de Chile signed a six-year, $315 million loan from seven foreign banks, the company said Friday.</p>
<p>The money will be used to finance ''CTC's investment plans for the first half of 1997 and for amortization of debt,'' said CTC in a statement.</p>
<p>Under the loan, which a CTC statement called a ''club deal'', each one of the banks pledged $45 million under identical conditions. The final syndication of the loan will be finished within 90 days, it said.</p>
</text>
